From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:41:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] venus/android: leave VK_KHR_device_address_commands to a
 platform that lists it

Android's CTS fails a device that exposes a KHR extension its release does not
list: VulkanDeqpLevelTest#testVulkanExposedDeviceExtensions compares every
advertised device extension with the set dEQP-VK knows for the declared level.
VK_KHR_device_address_commands is newer than the CTS releases the product is
tested with, so a device declaring android.software.vulkan.deqp.level at any
level fails that case on this one extension and on nothing else.

Pass the extension through everywhere but Android. It returns to Android with
the CTS release that lists it, and no Android application of the product asks
for it before then.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
index a9d6c71142e913edd8e8d9d3e772a8813ee56b97..cd6af3bc66004bde1e2338be8c08dfb8c74cd49a 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_physical_device.c
@@ -1335,7 +1335,12 @@ vn_physical_device_get_passthrough_extensions(
       .KHR_compute_shader_derivatives = true,
       .KHR_cooperative_matrix = true,
       .KHR_depth_clamp_zero_one = true,
+#ifndef VK_USE_PLATFORM_ANDROID_KHR
+      /* Android's CTS fails a device that exposes a KHR extension its release
+       * does not list (VulkanDeqpLevelTest#testVulkanExposedDeviceExtensions),
+       * and the CTS this product is tested with predates this extension. */
       .KHR_device_address_commands = true,
+#endif
       .KHR_fragment_shader_barycentric = true,
       .KHR_fragment_shading_rate = true,
       .KHR_maintenance7 =
